  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact 23-0001238 Creating an enabling refugee protection environment for LGBTQI+ Asylum Seekers in the African region.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact 23-0001238 This project focuses on advocating for the rights of the LGBTQI+ asylum seekers living in South Africa with the aim of influencing government to change and/ or adopt policies that will ensure that the process of asylum is more LGBTQI+ friendly. Through this project the LRC will offer legal representation to LGBTQI+ asylum seekers as well as work with other public interest organisations to advocate for the rights of the LGBTQI+ asylum seekers living in South Africa with the aim of influencing government to change and/ or adopt policies that will ensure that the process of asylum is more LGBTQI+ friendly. The project also seeks to develop a network of public interest organisations in the African region, particularly from refugee producing countries that continue to persecute the LGBTQI+ community with the aim of sharing  expertise and advocacy strategies.</narrative>
  </description>
